From: Mihawk <163614687+mihawk-99@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 01 Nov 2026 14:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] server: PS5: The title types text as Unicode keys.

A game that asks for text has no keyboard unless one is plugged in. The title's on-screen keyboard (the system's IME dialog,
opened by a trigger the player chose in Settings) returns a line of text, which has to reach the game as typing. The input
the title injects (patch 0931, 1001, 2418) had keys by virtual key only, and most characters have none on the key
layout the console is set to (accents, Cyrillic, CJK). A new input type, 10 (PW_WINE_INPUT_CHAR), carries one UTF-16 unit as a
KEYEVENTF_UNICODE key: the server queues it as a VK_PACKET key for the focused window (queue_keyboard_message already
turns that into WM_CHAR), and the in-process driver sends the same with NtUserSendHardwareInput. down 1 and down 0 are
the key's press and release.

The idea of typing the accepted line into the game was found by reading prospero-win (mpereiraesaa/prospero-win,
LGPL-2.1-or-later; commit d5a1601, which types virtual keys for a US layout); the Unicode route is written independently
here (NOTICE.md, "prospero-win and ProsperoMC"). Not run on a console.
---
 dlls/win32u/ps5drv.c |  8 ++++++++
 server/queue.c       | 10 ++++++++++
 2 files changed, 18 insertions(+)

diff --git a/dlls/win32u/ps5drv.c b/dlls/win32u/ps5drv.c
index 34d7385..04958e6 100644
--- a/dlls/win32u/ps5drv.c
+++ b/dlls/win32u/ps5drv.c
@@ -801,6 +801,14 @@ static BOOL ps5_ProcessEvents( DWORD mask )
                 NtUserSendHardwareInput( hwnd, 0, &button, 0 );
             }
             break;
+        case 10:
+            /* one UTF-16 unit of typed text (the on-screen keyboard's) */
+            if (!event.code || event.code > 0xffff) break;
+            input.ki.wVk = 0;
+            input.ki.wScan = event.code;
+            input.ki.dwFlags = KEYEVENTF_UNICODE | (event.down ? 0 : KEYEVENTF_KEYUP);
+            NtUserSendHardwareInput( hwnd, 0, &input, 0 );
+            break;
         case 6:
         {
             /* the wheels, in WHEEL_DELTA units */
diff --git a/server/queue.c b/server/queue.c
index e7596ab..8543638 100644
--- a/server/queue.c
+++ b/server/queue.c
@@ -3539,6 +3539,16 @@ void ps5_inject_input( unsigned int type, unsigned int code, int x, int y, unsig
         if (code >= 3) input.mouse.data = code == 3 ? XBUTTON1 : XBUTTON2;
         queue_mouse_message( desktop, 0, &input, IMO_HARDWARE, NULL, 0 );
         break;
+    case 10:
+        /* one UTF-16 unit of typed text (the on-screen keyboard's), as a KEYEVENTF_UNICODE key: it reaches the focused
+         * window as a VK_PACKET key, then WM_CHAR, as a text-input device's would */
+        if (!code || code > 0xffff) break;
+        input.kbd.type  = INPUT_KEYBOARD;
+        input.kbd.vkey  = 0;
+        input.kbd.scan  = code;
+        input.kbd.flags = KEYEVENTF_UNICODE | (down ? 0 : KEYEVENTF_KEYUP);
+        queue_keyboard_message( desktop, 0, &input, IMO_HARDWARE, NULL, 0, 0 );
+        break;
     case 7:
     {
         /* one process, named by its native helper's pid (code), for the title's memory guard in the desktop session:
